Subject: [PATCH] Reject partial sysroot metadata

During cross compilation, partial sysroot metadata may be present.
This patch ensures that any partial metadata results in an error.

This patch was generated with the assistance of AI.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe specific]

Signed-off-by: Jean-Marc BOUCHE <jean-marc.bouche@foss.st.com>

Index: ra_ap_project_model-0.0.295/src/sysroot.rs
===================================================================
--- ra_ap_project_model-0.0.295.orig/src/sysroot.rs	2006-07-24 03:21:28.000000000 +0200
+++ ra_ap_project_model-0.0.295/src/sysroot.rs	2026-10-30 13:30:53.533451609 +0100
@@ -337,9 +337,12 @@
 
         // Make sure we never attempt to write to the sysroot
         let locked = true;
-        let (mut res, _) =
+        let (mut res, metadata_error) =
             FetchMetadata::new(library_manifest, current_dir, &cargo_config, self, no_deps)
                 .exec(target_dir, locked, progress)?;
+        if let Some(error) = metadata_error {
+            return Err(error);
+        }
 
         // Patch out `rustc-std-workspace-*` crates to point to the real crates.
         // This is done prior to `CrateGraph` construction to prevent de-duplication logic from failing.
